> Table~\ref{tab:traces} splits the 768-token gap using the trace's own written values. Arithmetic is a large share only for Granite-8B, about a fifth of its gap. For every model, most of the loss comes after the best option's value is already on the page: the answer takes another bid. For the Qwen models this happens mostly in unfinished lists, for Phi-mini and Granite-8B in finished ones. With the match tolerance at 1\% instead of 2\% no share moves by more than 4 points, and at 5\% by at most 11, with the same dominant category for every model. Even counting a trace as Passed only when both the matcher and the text reader find every value, Passed remains the largest share for Phi-mini (71\%) and Granite-8B (51\%). The split also holds outside Cartier, in dollars and with the categories assigned in a different order, and passing over is rarer when the best option leads the runner-up by more.
